@startuml GaussSeidel_Algorithm

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam participantPadding 100
skinparam wrapWidth 0
skinparam maxMessageSize 500

participant "Master/\nOrchestrator" as Master
participant "SU₁\n(Gen 0)" as SU1
participant "SU₂\n(Gen 1)" as SU2

== Gauss-Seidel Co-Simulation: One Step t → t+dt ==

Master -> Master: **For each generation sequentially**

note over Master: **Generation 0: Process SU₁**

Master -> SU1: **1. Set inputs** from connections
activate SU1
note right: Use outputs from\nprevious time step
SU1 --> Master: inputs set
deactivate SU1

alt SU₁ in algebraic loop
    Master -> SU1: **2. Solve algebraic loop** (IJCSA)
    activate SU1
    note right: Interface-Newton iteration\nto resolve coupling
    SU1 --> Master: converged
    deactivate SU1
end

Master -> SU1: **3. Execute time step** do_step(t, dt)
activate SU1
SU1 -> SU1: Integrate t → t+dt
SU1 -> SU1: Update outputs at t+dt
SU1 --> Master: Y₁(t+dt) available
deactivate SU1

note over Master: **Generation 1: Process SU₂**

Master -> SU2: **1. Set inputs** from connections
activate SU2
note right: Use **fresh** Y₁(t+dt)\nfrom SU₁
SU2 --> Master: inputs set
deactivate SU2

alt SU₂ in algebraic loop
    Master -> SU2: **2. Solve algebraic loop** (IJCSA)
    activate SU2
    SU2 --> Master: converged
    deactivate SU2
end

Master -> SU2: **3. Execute time step** do_step(t, dt)
activate SU2
SU2 -> SU2: Integrate t → t+dt
SU2 -> SU2: Update outputs at t+dt
SU2 --> Master: Y₂(t+dt) available
deactivate SU2

Master -> Master: All generations complete\nt ← t + dt

' note over Master, SU2
' **Gauss-Seidel Properties:**
' • Sequential execution by generation
' • Later components use updated outputs from earlier ones
' • Reduced phase lag compared to Jacobi
' • No parallelism within generation
' • Algebraic loops solved via IJCSA before time step
' end note

@enduml